// Endpoint posture ceiling: propose a pause when the share of monitored endpoints
// outside their approved security posture reaches 15 percent. The hold half of a
// pair. ENDPOINT_NONCOMPLIANT_PCT is the percentage of in-scope endpoints the
// host currently measures as out of posture.
// REGIME: all of them, while the fleet is in service.
// CONDITIONS: none in the rule. The host defines approved posture, decides which
// endpoints are in scope, measures compliance and does anything about it. Nano
// cannot scan or quarantine an endpoint, and the pause is a proposal for the
// host's DecisionGate.
// INVALIDATION: remediation bringing the share back under 15 percent. No latch;
// the host decides when the hold ends.
// SHAPE: 1h, matching the advisory rule so both read the same measurement.
// NOT endpoint_posture_drift: that is the same signal at 5 percent and it only
// asks for review. This one says drift has become a fleet-wide condition worth
// holding work for. Above 15 percent both fire, which is intended: the review
// record continues alongside the hold.
// CALIBRATED ON: policy, not data. 15 percent is a placeholder hold line, three
// times the review line; keep the ratio when a site moves either figure.
strategy EndpointPostureCeiling {

    agent SecurityDesk

    every 1h {

        if ENDPOINT_NONCOMPLIANT_PCT >= 15 {

            pause()

        }

    }

}
